{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And Amalek came.</b> At the sound of quarreling and thirst, as it says: וְאַתָּה עָיֵף וְיָגֵעַ (Deuteronomy 25:18) — like וְאַתָּה עָיֵף וְיָגֵעַ in the sense of לֹא מַיִם עָיֵף תַּשְׁקֶה (Job 22:7), and like בְּאֶרֶץ עֲיֵפָה (Isaiah 32:2)."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {0 "Sforno's point is that Amalek attacked when Israel was weary (עיף) from the quarrel and thirst; he cites three verses using the ע-י-פ root to support reading ואתה עיף ויגע as describing the circumstances. The second citation reference appears to be a copyist insertion or cross-reference to the lemma verse itself (Deut. 25:18); translated as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:25:59.681318385Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}